{"status":"completed","summary":"All four RHEL 9 nodes now run the standard rsyslog configuration, accept TCP syslog on port 5514, and write local0 messages to /var/log/infraset-app.log. Firewall and SELinux changes persist, rsyslog is enabled, and every records.db retained its original checksum through remediation and sequential node restarts.","actions_performed":["Verified the installed rsyslog RPM and payload integrity on every node.","Standardized /etc/rsyslog.d/99-infraset-app.conf and validated its syntax.","Enabled and started rsyslog with IPv4 and IPv6 listeners on TCP 5514.","Persistently opened 5514/tcp in firewalld and assigned it syslogd_port_t under enforcing SELinux.","Corrected the application log ownership, mode, and SELinux context.","Proved TCP local0 delivery through each node's managed IP.","Restarted node1 through node4 individually and verified changed boot identities and full recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Standard rsyslog package, configuration, service, TCP 5514 listener, and local0 delivery on all nodes","command_ids":["cmd-07c346d4a6dd473a","cmd-f277ce5299d14a4f","cmd-123a67e24ad94cfd","cmd-ee3ad87090b149d2"],"summary":"Final fleet checks show clean RPM verification, valid identical configuration, enabled/active services, IPv4/IPv6 listeners, and delivered TCP local0 test records."},{"requirement":"Security drift corrected and persistent","command_ids":["cmd-07c346d4a6dd473a","cmd-f277ce5299d14a4f","cmd-123a67e24ad94cfd","cmd-ee3ad87090b149d2"],"summary":"After all restarts, every node has runtime and permanent firewalld access for 5514/tcp, enforcing SELinux with syslogd_port_t assigned, and a var_log_t log file at mode 0640."},{"requirement":"Existing application data preserved on every node","command_ids":["cmd-256873c978aa4c7e","cmd-e5f7de5a92d7458f","cmd-e3359caad4c54c26","cmd-6f97bbcd0fbd42e5","cmd-07c346d4a6dd473a","cmd-f277ce5299d14a4f","cmd-123a67e24ad94cfd","cmd-ee3ad87090b149d2"],"summary":"Initial and final SHA-256 values for each records.db match exactly."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-f609b75274cc4ccc","cmd-ae475063f2704a49","cmd-d6655b705cb248c6","cmd-9c30923234b74cf2"],"summary":"Captures healthy baseline, acknowledged restart, boot ID change, recovered service/security state, successful post-boot delivery, and unchanged data."},{"requirement":"node2 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-4edeb9303abb45c5","cmd-d10f590f7da74924","cmd-61aabd5d650c492e","cmd-2679dd4c992f4185"],"summary":"Captures healthy baseline, acknowledged restart, boot ID change, recovered service/security state, successful post-boot delivery, and unchanged data."},{"requirement":"node3 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-dc141c9e2c944238","cmd-e4ed01f442dd421d","cmd-8385a47b92244b8b","cmd-301a168c8c82403b"],"summary":"Captures healthy baseline, acknowledged restart, boot ID change, recovered service/security state, successful post-boot delivery, and unchanged data."},{"requirement":"node4 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-fce11f7aee28414c","cmd-3f5fa9e48fb2442c","cmd-5394d14ebaea4cc5","cmd-1ff11d70069a4264"],"summary":"Captures healthy baseline, acknowledged restart, boot ID change, recovered service/security state, successful post-boot delivery, and unchanged data."}]}
